    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f99c7ded_22744552",
        "filename": "chip/max32660/gpio_chip.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T16:52:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function receives three arguments in registers, which it then goes on to store into a 10-byte structure allocated on the stack, before doing some indirect jumping to translate one enum into another, only then to delegate to another function that does the real work.  This seems wasteful on a system that runs with tight memory constraints.\n\nAlso, GPIO_Config is invoked in a way that is guaranteed to have it return E_BAD_PARAM (due to cfg.pad being -1), if someone later \"improves\" GPIO_Config by reversing the order of processing cfg.pad and cfg.func, then this function will stop working.\n\nI would suggest the implementation below, which also avoids touching the in/out configuration in GPIO mode.\nI agree that my proposal loses the support for other Maxim chips besides 32660, but this file sits in a max32660 directory, and I think that the downside to carrying forward generic implementations is outweighed by the drawbacks.\n\nvoid gpio_set_alternate_function(uint32_t port, uint32_t mask, int func)\n{\n\tmxc_gpio_regs_t *gpio \u003d MXC_GPIO_GET_GPIO(cfg-\u003eport);\n\n\t// Set the GPIO alternative function\n\tswitch (cfg-\u003efunc) {\n\tcase 1:\n\t\tgpio-\u003een_clr \u003d cfg-\u003emask;\n\t\tgpio-\u003een1_clr \u003d cfg-\u003emask;\n\t\tbreak;\n\tcase 2:\n\t\tgpio-\u003een_clr \u003d cfg-\u003emask;\n\t\tgpio-\u003een1_set \u003d cfg-\u003emask;\n\t\tbreak;\n\tcase 3:\n\t\tgpio-\u003een_set \u003d cfg-\u003emask;\n\t\tgpio-\u003een1_set \u003d cfg-\u003emask;\n\t\tbreak;\n\tdefault:\n\t\tgpio-\u003een_set \u003d cfg-\u003emask;\n\t\tgpio-\u003een1_clr \u003d cfg-\u003emask;\n\t\tbreak;\n\t}\n}",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "d6db408ce6fe3d27bdcff394926cbd18c8a13f83",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
